INT. WAYNE MANOR - DAY

ANDREA stands in the study, looking over some case files. ALFRED enters, holding a tray with tea.

ALFRED
Master Andrea, I've noticed you've been quite engrossed in your work. Perhaps a moment of respite? And I might have some insights that could be of use.

ANDREA
(Takes a cup of tea)
Thank you, Alfred. I appreciate it. I could use some advice.

ALFRED
(Smiling slightly)
Sometimes, the smallest details are the most telling. Don't overlook the obvious, and always consider the human element. It's not always about the facts, but the motivations behind them.

Andrea nods, taking in Alfred's words. He then heads to the Batcave, where he accesses the city's crime database. He finds a recent string of robberies with a strange pattern.

ANDREA
(To himself)
This is odd. The locations, the timing... it doesn't make sense.

He decides to investigate the most recent crime scene, a jewelry store downtown.
===GAME END===
