INT. GOTHAM CITY STREETS - DAY

Andrea arrives at the third crime scene, a small bookstore. The door is forced open, and books are scattered everywhere. He steps inside, carefully navigating the mess.

ANDREA
(Observing the scene)
This is different from the others. Not as much damage, but still...

He notices that some of the books are missing, specifically first editions and rare manuscripts. He also finds a small, almost invisible symbol etched into the wooden floor near the entrance. It's a circle with a line through it, unlike anything he's seen before.

ANDREA
(Thinking)
This symbol... it's a pattern.

He takes detailed photos of the symbol and the overall scene, noting the specific books that are missing. He also finds a small, torn piece of paper near the back of the store, with a series of numbers written on it. He carefully collects it, adding it to his evidence.

ANDREA
(To himself)
This is more than just random robberies. There's a purpose here.

He exits the bookstore, deciding to head back to the Batcave to analyze the new evidence.
===GAME END===
