ANDREA
(Looking around)
This is... different.

He notices that several paintings are missing, but not just any paintings. They are all pieces with a specific recurring motif: a stylized depiction of a serpent. He also finds a small, almost invisible symbol etched into the back of one of the empty frames, the same circle with a line through it that he saw at the bookstore.

ANDREA
(Thinking)
The same symbol again. This is definitely connected.

He takes detailed photos of the symbol, the empty frames, and the overall scene, noting the specific paintings that are missing. He also finds a small, almost invisible, piece of dark fabric snagged on a broken display case, similar to the one he found at the jewelry store. He carefully collects it, adding it to his evidence.

ANDREA
(To himself)
This is all connected. The symbol, the fabric... it's a pattern.

He exits the art gallery, deciding to head back to the Batcave to analyze the new evidence.
