INT. WAYNE MANOR - NIGHT

Andrea returns to Wayne Manor, feeling the exhaustion of his recent investigations. The manor is quiet and peaceful, a stark contrast to the chaos of Gotham's streets and the unsettling atmosphere of Arkham Asylum. He heads to his room, where he can finally relax and recover.

ANDREA
(To himself)
I need to clear my head.

He takes a shower, changes into comfortable clothes, and lies down on the bed. The soft mattress and the quiet surroundings help him to unwind. He closes his eyes, letting the stress of the day melt away. He drifts off to sleep, his mind finally at peace.

He wakes up feeling refreshed and rejuvenated, ready to continue his investigation. He knows that the mastermind behind the recent crimes is still out there, and he needs to be prepared for whatever comes next.
