INT. THE BATCAVE - NIGHT

Andrea descends into the Batcave, the high-tech environment a stark contrast to the old-world charm of Wayne Manor. He lays out all the evidence he's collected: photos of the crime scenes, the scratch mark, the fabric samples, the torn piece of paper with numbers, and the notes from his conversation with Silas and The Serpent.

ANDREA
(To himself)
Time to put the pieces together.

He starts by analyzing the fabric samples, using the Batcave's advanced equipment. He discovers that the fabric is made of a rare, synthetic material, not something commonly found in Gotham. He then analyzes the scratch mark, finding that it was made by a specific type of tool, a custom-made lock pick. He also uses the Batcomputer to decipher the numbers on the torn piece of paper, discovering that they are coordinates to a location on the outskirts of Gotham.

ANDREA
(Thinking)
This is it. This is where they're hiding.

He decides to upgrade his equipment, spending some of his resources to enhance his detective tools. He also plans his next move, knowing that he needs to be prepared for a confrontation.
