EXT. STREETS OF MANHATTAN - NIGHT

Alex leaves the lair, feeling refreshed. He receives another comm from Marc.

MARC
(urgently)
Alex, another crime scene. This one's a bit different. Looks like a warehouse break-in.

ALEX
(responding)
On my way.

Alex arrives at the warehouse, a large, imposing structure with a broken loading dock door. He carefully enters the building, his flashlight beam cutting through the darkness. The warehouse is filled with crates and boxes, many of them overturned. He notices a trail of footprints leading deeper into the building. He also finds a small, torn piece of paper with a symbol on it.

Suddenly, a figure emerges from behind a stack of crates, wielding a pipe.

CRIMINAL
(shouting)
You shouldn't have come here!

Alex quickly assesses the situation, ready to fight.

ALEX
(firmly)
Drop the pipe!

The criminal lunges forward, and Alex engages in a brief but intense struggle. Alex manages to disarm and subdue the criminal.
